WEBVTT

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:07.870
Citizens of Earth,
your destiny is in my hands.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:11.342
Those of you who acquiesce
to my demands

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:13.936
will be treated fairly.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.744
Oppose me, and you face
a dire fate indeed

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:23.050
as my slaves in the mines
of Mercury.

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:25.956
You have one hour.

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.323
You'll never get away with this.

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:29.919
Oh, but I shall.

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:33.329
Your once-proud country
will fall to its knees.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.892
How ironic that I am
using your rocket ship

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:41.066
to lead my space force
into battle.

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:42.768
You're wrong, Chaotica.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.400
Before you came on board,

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.968
someone pushed
the self-destruct button.

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:49.638
In three minutes,
we'll all be dead.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.081
No!

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:55.154
The jig is up, Your Majesty.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.985
Captain Proton.

00:00:58.091 --> 00:01:01.288
Spaceman First Class,
Protector of Earth

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:05.798
Scourge of Intergalactic Evil...
at your service.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.924
But I saw you fall
into the fiery mouth

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:09.126
of that volcano.

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:12.262
It takes more than a little lava
to stop Captain Proton.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:16.297
Now, I want you to call off
your invasion

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:19.174
and give me back my rocket ship.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.475
There is one force
in this universe

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.379
that even you cannot defeat.

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:27.617
The same to you.

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:28.619
Doc.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:29.620
Mr. Paris.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:30.621
I should have known

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.123
it was you
monopolizing the holodeck.

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.660
Who is this insolent fool?

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:37.662
Uh, he's one of our men.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.823
Computer, adjust the Doctor's
spectral frequency.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:42.197
I have no interest
in your frivolous fantasy.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.736
I'm here to rehearse a duet
from Don Carlo

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.931
and you've already gone
three minutes into my sched...

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:47.973
Enough!

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:49.666
Robot, attack.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:54.641
Destroy them.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.272
Start with him.

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.907
Computer, freeze program.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.552
Doc, this is the final chapter...

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:05.182
"Satan's Robot
Conquers the World."

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:06.316
We can't stop now.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.383
Does the phrase
"to be continued"

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.723
mean anything to you?

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:10.728
Your opera can wait.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:13.027
This program is a waste
of photonic energy.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:14.031
Oh, really?

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.499
Take a look around you.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:18.298
This is how the 20th century
saw the future.

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:19.633
We are studying sociology.

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:22.334
Perhaps you can teach a course
at Starfleet Academy...

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:25.571
"Satan's Robot:
An historical overview."

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.480
Bridge to Holodeck 1.

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.109
What's going on down there?

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:34.744
Oh, nothing, Commander.

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.652
Just a little power surge.

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:38.691
Says here the hologrid
just blew out.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.316
We're fixing it now, sir.

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:41.587
Well, make it quick.

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:44.357
The last thing we need
is a broken holodeck.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.261
Seven, I want good news.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:47.560
That's an order.

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.965
Then I must disobey.

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:50.969
I have no good news to report.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:54.164
I've completed an astrometric
scan of the entire region.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.834
There are no star systems
within 2,500 light-years.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:57.842
Nothing?

00:02:57.911 --> 00:02:58.843
Nothing.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.846
Why can't we see any stars
beyond that?

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:03.439
There are heavy concentrations
of theta radiation.

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:04.915
It has occluded our sensors.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:06.349
Any other ships out there?

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:08.216
None. We are alone.

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:12.455
Every sailor's nightmare.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.083
Commander?

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.890
It's like being becalmed
in the middle of the ocean.

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:18.260
If it weren't for sensors,

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:20.322
we wouldn't even know
we were at warp.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.868
We've only been crossing
this expanse for two months

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:24.563
and we're already feeling
the strain.

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.070
How do we last
another two years?

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:28.767
We will adapt.

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:30.832
Easier said than done.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:34.641
Shall I inform
the Captain of my findings?

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:37.948
No.

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:40.052
I'll tell her.

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:46.067
First Officer's Log,
Stardate 52081.2.

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:49.342
It's been 53 days since we
entered this desolate region.

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:51.406
If we want to continue
our course toward home,

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:53.611
we have no choice
but to cross it.

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:56.587
We won't have an opportunity to
take on fresh supplies or fuel,

00:05:56.656 --> 00:05:59.591
so I've ordered all departments
to create an energy reserve.

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:02.651
We're using power cells
to stockpile deuterium.

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:04.663
This won't be much
of a briefing.

00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:06.198
There's nothing new to report.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:08.461
Humor me.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.001
All right. Let's see.

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:12.128
Warp core's at peak efficiency,

00:06:12.205 --> 00:06:15.470
just like last week
and the week before that.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:18.203
And my Engineering staff
is going stir-crazy.

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:19.767
Thanks.

00:06:19.846 --> 00:06:20.778
Ensign?

00:06:20.847 --> 00:06:22.712
Nada.

00:06:22.782 --> 00:06:24.773
Can you be more specific?

00:06:24.851 --> 00:06:27.877
All systems are operating
within normal parameters.

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:29.888
Anything new on sensors?

00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:32.117
I detected a sudden increase
of theta radiation

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:33.123
in the vicinity.

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:33.920
Source?

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:35.152
Unknown.

00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:36.490
Could be worth a look.

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:38.393
Finally, some excitement...

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:40.329
radiation.

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:44.359
Next piece of business.

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:45.734
Crew morale.

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:47.432
Deteriorating...

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:48.667
obviously.

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:50.106
I have a few suggestions

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:52.144
that might boost
people's spirits.

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:53.371
Please.

00:06:53.446 --> 00:06:55.641
Rotate crew assignments.

00:06:55.715 --> 00:06:58.684
Add variety
to the daily routine.

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:00.582
I myself wouldn't mind
squeezing in

00:07:00.653 --> 00:07:02.143
a little tactical training.

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:04.189
Noted.

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:07.055
And the holodecks
have been in high demand.

00:07:07.126 --> 00:07:09.720
I was thinking...
we could install a few emitters

00:07:09.796 --> 00:07:10.763
in Cargo Bay 2...

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.457
turn it into a third holodeck.

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:13.499
Hear, hear.

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:15.056
See to it, Harry.

00:07:15.134 --> 00:07:16.726
One other item, sir.

00:07:16.803 --> 00:07:20.569
Point of, uh, concern
among some of the crew.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.267
It's...

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:23.672
Well, it's the Captain.

00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:25.574
She's been a bit elusive lately.

00:07:25.645 --> 00:07:27.579
What's your point?

00:07:27.647 --> 00:07:29.581
People take comfort
in talking to her.

00:07:29.649 --> 00:07:32.447
When they see that the Captain's
happy, they're happy.

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:34.918
Rumor has it
she never leaves her quarters.

00:07:34.987 --> 00:07:36.045
Captain's privilege.

00:07:36.122 --> 00:07:38.181
She'll come to the Bridge
if and when she's needed.

00:07:38.257 --> 00:07:39.485
Spare us the protocol, Chakotay.

00:07:39.559 --> 00:07:41.186
It's pretty odd,
you've got to admit it.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:42.192
It's her choice.

00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:43.353
She can run this ship

00:07:43.429 --> 00:07:44.828
from wherever the hell
she wants to.

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:45.864
Understood?

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:48.930
Yeah.

00:07:49.068 --> 00:07:50.592
Sure.

00:07:51.838 --> 00:07:55.706
We're all feeling the pressure,
including me.

00:07:55.775 --> 00:07:58.869
Listen, maybe we've got
the wrong attitude.

00:07:58.945 --> 00:08:02.108
Let's think of this
as a two-year vacation.

00:08:04.951 --> 00:08:06.043
Dismissed.

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:08.643
That's a great idea, Harry.

00:08:08.721 --> 00:08:09.653
Wow, Harry.

00:08:09.722 --> 00:08:10.984
You're a real genius.

00:08:11.057 --> 00:08:13.150
How do you come up
with these brilliant ideas?

00:08:13.226 --> 00:08:14.784
You're such an optimistic guy.

00:08:44.257 --> 00:08:47.818
Computer, lights...
maximum level.

00:08:47.894 --> 00:08:50.021
Bergamot tea, hot.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:15.181
First thing in the morning,
I replicate some curtains.

00:09:23.062 --> 00:09:24.495
Predictable.

00:09:24.564 --> 00:09:25.997
Hmm?

00:09:26.065 --> 00:09:29.228
The Novokovich gambit... you
always use that opening move.

00:09:29.302 --> 00:09:31.497
That's because you always
fall for it.

00:09:31.571 --> 00:09:34.904
I feel like we've played
this match a hundred times.

00:09:35.041 --> 00:09:38.374
Derada is a game of subtlety.

00:09:38.444 --> 00:09:39.775
Too subtle for me.

00:09:39.845 --> 00:09:43.372
Hmm. I'll bet.

00:09:43.449 --> 00:09:44.848
What's that supposed to mean?

00:09:44.917 --> 00:09:49.013
Well, if it doesn't involve
Klingon painsticks...

00:09:49.088 --> 00:09:50.020
Good night.

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:53.181
There you go.
Just when I'm winning.

00:09:53.259 --> 00:09:54.487
Who's predictable?

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:56.357
You don't want to start a fight
with me right now...

00:09:56.429 --> 00:09:57.361
not at 3:00 A.M.

00:09:57.430 --> 00:10:00.160
3:00 in the morning,
4:00 in the afternoon...

00:10:00.232 --> 00:10:01.290
what's the difference?

00:10:01.367 --> 00:10:02.732
You're angry 24 hours a day.

00:10:02.802 --> 00:10:04.133
Everything is a joke to you.

00:10:04.203 --> 00:10:06.569
Good evening...
or should I say good morning?

00:10:06.639 --> 00:10:08.766
I guess you couldn't
sleep, either.

00:10:08.841 --> 00:10:11.332
Why sleep when we're
having so much fun?

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:13.537
He's joking, Neelix.
We're all supposed to laugh.

00:10:13.613 --> 00:10:15.046
I certainly am laughing

00:10:15.114 --> 00:10:17.674
on the inside...
smiling, anyway.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:20.184
Let's start a new game.
Cards?

00:10:20.252 --> 00:10:21.617
A little snack?

00:10:21.687 --> 00:10:23.518
No. I have a better idea.

00:10:23.589 --> 00:10:27.116
Why don't we make a schedule...
a fight rotation?

00:10:27.193 --> 00:10:28.455
We can optimize our resources.

00:10:28.527 --> 00:10:30.358
I can start one,
then you can start one...

00:10:30.429 --> 00:10:31.919
Please...

00:10:31.998 --> 00:10:33.590
I am really tired
of these games.

00:10:33.666 --> 00:10:35.065
Well, then don't play them.

00:10:35.134 --> 00:10:36.066
Stop!

00:10:36.135 --> 00:10:38.535
You are senior officers!

00:10:38.604 --> 00:10:41.801
You are supposed to be setting
an example for the rest...

00:10:41.874 --> 00:10:44.308
the rest of the crew.

00:10:45.544 --> 00:10:46.476
Neelix?

00:10:46.545 --> 00:10:47.876
I can't breathe.

00:10:47.947 --> 00:10:49.539
Paris to Sick Bay.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:53.651
Some morale officer
I turned out to be.

00:10:53.719 --> 00:10:55.983
I've given you a mild sedative.

00:10:56.088 --> 00:10:59.421
It should control
the urge to hyperventilate

00:10:59.492 --> 00:11:02.086
and alleviate
some of your anxiety.

00:11:02.161 --> 00:11:06.291
Anxiety? Anxiety's what I feel
when I burn a pot roast.

00:11:06.365 --> 00:11:08.390
This... this is more like...

00:11:08.467 --> 00:11:10.901
Dizziness? Nausea?
Unspeakable dread?

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:12.301
Yes.

00:11:12.371 --> 00:11:14.362
Nihiliphobia...
the fear of nothingness,

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.203
or in layman's terms,
the fear of...

00:11:16.275 --> 00:11:17.401
nothingness.

00:11:17.476 --> 00:11:20.343
If it's any consolation,
I can relate to it.

00:11:20.413 --> 00:11:23.280
I go into a void every
time I'm deactivated...

00:11:23.349 --> 00:11:25.874
emptiness, complete
and utter oblivion.

00:11:25.951 --> 00:11:28.579
I'll admit, it was
unsettling at first...

00:11:28.654 --> 00:11:30.918
the existential horror
of it all...

00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:32.514
You're not helping, Doctor.

00:11:32.591 --> 00:11:34.354
Sorry.

00:11:34.427 --> 00:11:38.056
My point is,
you'll get used to it.

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:39.620
I hope so.

00:11:45.504 --> 00:11:46.698
Commander...

00:11:46.772 --> 00:11:48.763
am I disturbing you?

00:11:48.841 --> 00:11:50.365
No.

00:11:50.443 --> 00:11:54.539
Is the Astrometrics Lab
designated for recreational use?

00:11:54.613 --> 00:11:56.444
I come here to meditate.

00:11:56.515 --> 00:11:58.847
Needless to say,
the view from my quarters

00:11:58.918 --> 00:12:00.818
has been less
than stellar lately.

00:12:00.886 --> 00:12:04.413
Astronomical phenomena
help you to focus your mind.

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:09.621
Yes. I imagine that each star
represents a single thought.

00:12:09.695 --> 00:12:13.222
Meditation...
it rejuvenates you?

00:12:13.299 --> 00:12:14.561
Indeed it does.

00:12:14.633 --> 00:12:16.601
I suggest you try
Borg regeneration.

00:12:16.669 --> 00:12:18.102
It's much more efficient.

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:20.104
A simple cortical implant
would be required.

00:12:20.172 --> 00:12:22.299
Another time, perhaps.

00:12:23.876 --> 00:12:25.707
What is it?

00:12:25.778 --> 00:12:26.802
Long-range sensors

00:12:26.879 --> 00:12:28.210
are detecting
more theta radiation.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:29.542
Dangerously high levels.

00:12:29.615 --> 00:12:31.344
Source?

00:12:31.417 --> 00:12:33.351
Unknown.

00:12:33.419 --> 00:12:36.411
It's probably nothing, just...
background theta radiation.

00:12:36.489 --> 00:12:38.423
But it could mean
there's someone nearby.

00:12:38.491 --> 00:12:40.391
Distance?

00:12:40.459 --> 00:12:43.690
Approximately 25 light-years.

00:12:43.763 --> 00:12:46.891
It's a long shot
but alter course.

00:12:46.966 --> 00:12:49.696
Yes, ma'am.

00:12:49.769 --> 00:12:51.862
If that's all, Commander...

00:12:51.937 --> 00:12:54.132
Actually, I'd like
to make a request.

00:12:54.206 --> 00:12:56.504
I've been saving up
my holodeck rations

00:12:56.575 --> 00:12:58.805
and I've got
three full hours coming.

00:12:58.878 --> 00:13:01.540
Any chance
I might persuade you to join me

00:13:01.614 --> 00:13:03.514
for a few rounds of Velocity?

00:13:03.582 --> 00:13:05.641
Lt'll help clear your mind.

00:13:05.718 --> 00:13:07.777
My mind is perfectly clear.

00:13:07.853 --> 00:13:11.289
Then what if I told you I'm
not leaving until you join me?

00:13:11.357 --> 00:13:13.552
I'd say, "Have a seat.
It'll be a while."

00:13:14.593 --> 00:13:16.652
Then I'll be blunt.

00:13:16.729 --> 00:13:18.162
You've picked a bad time

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:20.255
to isolate yourself
from the crew.

00:13:20.332 --> 00:13:23.927
This ship needs a Captain,
especially now.

00:13:24.003 --> 00:13:26.528
Would you be satisfied with

00:13:26.605 --> 00:13:29.165
"I'm just catching up
on some reading?"

00:13:30.209 --> 00:13:32.871
I'm not sure
I understand it myself.

00:13:32.945 --> 00:13:34.412
It started when we
entered this...

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:35.913
What does the crew call it?

00:13:35.981 --> 00:13:36.948
The Void.

00:13:37.016 --> 00:13:38.916
Charming.

00:13:38.984 --> 00:13:42.750
Oh, what I wouldn't give
for a few Borg cubes about now...

00:13:42.822 --> 00:13:45.188
anything for
a little distraction.

00:13:46.625 --> 00:13:49.150
Strange as it sounds...

00:13:49.228 --> 00:13:50.923
I almost long for the days

00:13:50.996 --> 00:13:53.260
when we were under
constant attack.

00:13:53.332 --> 00:13:54.663
No time to stop and think

00:13:54.733 --> 00:13:57.327
about how we got stranded
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:13:57.403 --> 00:13:59.200
How did we end up here,
Chakotay?

00:14:02.274 --> 00:14:03.468
Answer me.

00:14:05.511 --> 00:14:07.741
We were faced
with a difficult choice.

00:14:07.813 --> 00:14:09.678
We had the means to get home,

00:14:09.748 --> 00:14:12.478
but using it would have put
an innocent people at risk

00:14:12.551 --> 00:14:13.813
so we decided to stay.

00:14:13.886 --> 00:14:16.446
No... no, no.

00:14:16.522 --> 00:14:18.490
I decided to stay.

00:14:18.557 --> 00:14:20.650
I made that choice
for everyone.

00:14:20.726 --> 00:14:22.091
We're alive and well

00:14:22.161 --> 00:14:24.925
and we've gathered enough
data about this Quadrant

00:14:25.064 --> 00:14:27.897
to keep Starfleet scientists
busy for decades.

00:14:27.967 --> 00:14:30.800
Our mission's been a success.

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:32.838
Very same words
I've been telling myself

00:14:32.905 --> 00:14:35.032
for the past four years.

00:14:35.107 --> 00:14:37.735
But then we hit this Void,

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:41.769
and I started to realize
how empty those words sound.

00:14:41.847 --> 00:14:42.677
Kathryn...

00:14:42.748 --> 00:14:45.342
I made an error in judgment,
Chakotay.

00:14:45.417 --> 00:14:47.817
It was shortsighted
and it was selfish

00:14:47.887 --> 00:14:51.050
and now all of us
are paying for my mistake.

00:14:51.123 --> 00:14:54.024
So if you don't mind, Commander,
I'll pass on that little game.

00:14:55.995 --> 00:14:58.896
And I'll leave shipboard morale
in your capable hands.

00:15:02.067 --> 00:15:04.558
If the crew asks for me,

00:15:04.637 --> 00:15:08.004
tell them the Captain
sends her regards.

00:15:49.815 --> 00:15:51.180
Sir.

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:52.376
Relax, Ensign.

00:15:52.451 --> 00:15:53.918
Anything to report?

00:15:53.986 --> 00:15:55.886
Not even a stray electron,

00:15:55.955 --> 00:15:58.617
but I did finish
writing my concerto.

00:15:58.691 --> 00:16:00.921
I call it Echoes of the Void.

00:16:00.993 --> 00:16:02.722
Got a minute?

00:16:02.795 --> 00:16:04.353
Too many, in fact.

00:16:04.430 --> 00:16:06.489
Tell me what you think.

00:16:17.943 --> 00:16:20.104
Now, when we last saw
our heroes,

00:16:20.179 --> 00:16:22.841
they had just retaken
their rocket ship.

00:16:22.915 --> 00:16:24.746
Dr. Chaotica had escaped,

00:16:24.817 --> 00:16:27.377
but he left behind
his trusty robot

00:16:27.453 --> 00:16:29.478
to foil Captain Proton.

00:16:29.555 --> 00:16:31.420
My designation?

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:35.119
Ah, right.
You're Constance Goodheart.

00:16:35.194 --> 00:16:36.718
You're... my secretary.

00:16:36.795 --> 00:16:37.921
Secretary?

00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:40.624
Yeah. You tag along
on all the missions.

00:16:40.699 --> 00:16:43.190
Now, I want you to keep
the robot occupied

00:16:43.268 --> 00:16:44.530
while I save Earth.

00:16:44.603 --> 00:16:48.300
Computer, run program.

00:16:48.374 --> 00:16:50.865
Citizen of Earth, surrender.

00:16:50.943 --> 00:16:52.240
Do not resist.

00:16:52.311 --> 00:16:54.108
I am Borg.

00:16:54.179 --> 00:16:56.272
Surrender...

00:16:57.216 --> 00:16:59.184
The robot has been neutralized.

00:16:59.251 --> 00:17:00.343
May I leave now?

00:17:01.787 --> 00:17:03.015
Come on, Seven.

00:17:03.088 --> 00:17:04.715
Give it a chance.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:05.950
The galaxy's at stake.

00:17:17.569 --> 00:17:19.662
We've dropped out of warp.

00:17:19.738 --> 00:17:21.467
We're losing power.

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:23.007
Switch to auxiliary.

00:17:23.075 --> 00:17:24.599
No effect.

00:17:52.438 --> 00:17:54.633
I was hoping
for a change of pace,

00:17:54.706 --> 00:17:57.470
but a blackout isn't exactly
what I had in mind.

00:17:57.543 --> 00:18:00.410
I'll try tapping
into the energy reserves.

00:18:23.902 --> 00:18:25.529
Double-check the radio relay.

00:18:25.604 --> 00:18:26.628
Man the lock plate.

00:18:26.705 --> 00:18:28.070
Yeah, I'll get on that
right away.

00:18:38.117 --> 00:18:40.312
Get inside
those plasma injectors!

00:18:40.385 --> 00:18:42.785
Infuse them manually
if you have to.

00:18:42.855 --> 00:18:44.379
Lieutenant...

00:18:44.456 --> 00:18:45.889
Just a second.

00:18:45.958 --> 00:18:48.051
I'm not sure
how to work this thing.

00:18:53.465 --> 00:18:56.332
Captain Proton to the rescue.

00:18:56.401 --> 00:18:58.869
It's not exactly
Starfleet issue.

00:19:10.916 --> 00:19:13.350
Shipwide power loss?

00:19:13.418 --> 00:19:16.512
Everything's off-line...
main power, auxiliary...

00:19:16.588 --> 00:19:19.716
Independent subsystems
are operational...

00:19:19.791 --> 00:19:22.692
environmental controls,
holodecks...

00:19:22.761 --> 00:19:26.390
Reroute power from this holodeck
to the emergency relays.

00:19:27.432 --> 00:19:28.899
Yes, ma'am.

00:19:31.436 --> 00:19:32.869
No luck.

00:19:32.938 --> 00:19:34.735
The hologrid is frozen.

00:19:42.614 --> 00:19:44.081
Neelix.

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:47.042
Don't mind me.

00:19:47.119 --> 00:19:49.053
There's been a power loss.

00:19:49.121 --> 00:19:50.884
Nothing to worry about.

00:19:50.956 --> 00:19:52.548
Who's worried?

00:19:52.624 --> 00:19:54.057
Come on.

00:19:54.126 --> 00:19:57.562
Take deep breaths...
nice and slow.

00:19:57.629 --> 00:19:59.062
That's it.

00:20:00.465 --> 00:20:01.898
Bingo!

00:20:01.967 --> 00:20:03.594
We've got partial sensors.

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:10.370
I found the cause
of our power drain.

00:20:10.442 --> 00:20:12.467
It's some kind
of dampening field.

00:20:12.544 --> 00:20:14.409
The source is
off the port bow.

00:20:14.479 --> 00:20:16.413
That's about all I can tell you.

00:20:16.481 --> 00:20:17.880
On screen.

00:20:18.984 --> 00:20:22.750
Do we have the power
to launch a photon torpedo?

00:20:22.821 --> 00:20:24.755
Maybe one. Why?

00:20:24.823 --> 00:20:26.757
Perhaps we could
shed some light

00:20:26.825 --> 00:20:28.417
on our predicament.

00:20:28.493 --> 00:20:30.358
I'm reconfiguring the torpedo

00:20:30.429 --> 00:20:32.954
to emit a sustained
polyluminous burst.

00:20:33.031 --> 00:20:34.293
A "warp flare."

00:20:34.366 --> 00:20:35.799
Precisely.

00:20:43.008 --> 00:20:45.636
I need something
to pry open this hatch.

00:20:58.924 --> 00:21:02.451
Computer,
disengage safety protocols!

00:21:09.134 --> 00:21:10.567
I saw something!

00:21:10.636 --> 00:21:12.103
Over there.

00:21:16.975 --> 00:21:19.068
I'm telling you,
I saw something.

00:21:19.144 --> 00:21:22.602
I may be nihiliphobic,
but my eyes work just fine.

00:21:29.488 --> 00:21:31.456
I can hear breathing.

00:21:45.037 --> 00:21:46.402
Follow me.

00:21:46.471 --> 00:21:47.495
Yes, ma'am.

00:21:50.142 --> 00:21:52.440
Torpedo reconfigured.

00:21:52.511 --> 00:21:54.001
Away.

00:21:59.051 --> 00:22:00.916
I can barely see
the injector ports.

00:22:00.986 --> 00:22:02.817
How about a little light
over here?

00:22:02.888 --> 00:22:04.378
We can do better than that.

00:22:04.456 --> 00:22:06.287
This power cell should be enough

00:22:06.358 --> 00:22:08.383
to get emergency power
back on line.

00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:09.722
Up here!

00:22:09.795 --> 00:22:12.320
We'll hook it up directly
to the EPS manifold.

00:22:14.900 --> 00:22:16.891
Emergency power just came back.

00:22:16.968 --> 00:22:18.230
We've got tactical.

00:22:18.303 --> 00:22:19.600
Raising shields.

00:22:19.671 --> 00:22:22.401
The warp core's on line.

00:22:22.474 --> 00:22:23.907
Janeway to Bridge.
Report.

00:22:23.975 --> 00:22:26.569
The dampening field
has been blocked, Captain.

00:22:26.645 --> 00:22:28.704
We are surrounded
by three alien vessels.

00:22:28.780 --> 00:22:30.748
17 intruders are on board.

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:34.111
The ships aren't
responding to hails.

00:22:34.186 --> 00:22:36.177
We do have weapons on line.

00:22:36.254 --> 00:22:40.554
Tuvok, target the ship
off our port bow.

00:22:40.625 --> 00:22:42.855
Fire a few warning shots.

00:22:48.500 --> 00:22:50.593
Shields down to 64 percent.

00:22:50.669 --> 00:22:52.102
Do we have propulsion?

00:22:52.170 --> 00:22:53.637
Not yet.

00:22:55.774 --> 00:22:57.708
He was attacked by an intruder.

00:22:57.776 --> 00:22:58.970
These burns are severe.

00:22:59.111 --> 00:23:00.510
I disabled the alien.

00:23:00.579 --> 00:23:01.876
It may still be alive.

00:23:01.947 --> 00:23:03.437
Bring it to Sick Bay.

00:23:03.515 --> 00:23:05.244
Shields are down.

00:23:05.317 --> 00:23:07.217
They're reinitializing
the dampening field.

00:23:07.285 --> 00:23:08.445
We're losing power.

00:23:09.955 --> 00:23:11.422
Not again.

00:23:15.460 --> 00:23:17.325
They've stopped their attack.

00:23:17.396 --> 00:23:19.296
They're beaming off the ship.

00:23:19.364 --> 00:23:21.059
There's another vessel
approaching.

00:23:29.608 --> 00:23:30.939
We're being hailed.

00:23:31.042 --> 00:23:32.805
On screen.

00:23:33.945 --> 00:23:35.936
I'm Lieutenant Commander Tuvok
of the Federation...

00:23:36.081 --> 00:23:40.040
I had to fire 13 spatial charges
to drive those ships off.

00:23:40.118 --> 00:23:42.780
I expect to be compensated.

00:23:45.957 --> 00:23:47.254
Of course.

00:23:47.325 --> 00:23:48.952
Now...

00:23:49.094 --> 00:23:51.062
tell me...

00:23:51.129 --> 00:23:54.360
what are you doing
in the middle of nowhere?

00:24:03.408 --> 00:24:06.844
The bio-filters are detecting
high levels of theta radiation.

00:24:06.912 --> 00:24:08.038
Compensate.

00:24:10.182 --> 00:24:11.171
Welcome aboard.

00:24:11.249 --> 00:24:13.410
I'm afraid we'll have
to talk here.

00:24:13.485 --> 00:24:14.782
You appear to be leaking.

00:24:14.853 --> 00:24:17.481
Yes, yes. My isolation suit.

00:24:17.556 --> 00:24:19.148
Don't be alarmed.

00:24:19.224 --> 00:24:21.454
We'd prefer to be
on the safe side, Mister?

00:24:21.526 --> 00:24:22.788
Emck. Controller Emck,

00:24:22.861 --> 00:24:25.261
Malon export vessel,
eleventh gradient.

00:24:25.330 --> 00:24:26.922
It's a pleasure to meet you

00:24:27.032 --> 00:24:28.124
and a relief...

00:24:28.200 --> 00:24:30.464
I'd advise you
to turn around immediately.

00:24:30.535 --> 00:24:32.435
There are more
of those creatures ahead...

00:24:32.504 --> 00:24:33.493
thousands of vessels.

00:24:33.572 --> 00:24:36.598
They are almost impossible
to detect.

00:24:36.675 --> 00:24:38.336
You won't survive
another attack.

00:24:38.410 --> 00:24:39.775
We can't go back.

00:24:39.845 --> 00:24:43.508
We're crossing this
expanse to reach our home.

00:24:43.582 --> 00:24:45.709
Mmm.

00:24:45.784 --> 00:24:49.686
Then, uh... it appears
you'll be coming with me.

00:24:49.754 --> 00:24:50.743
What do you mean?

00:24:50.822 --> 00:24:53.950
There's a spatial vortex
a few light-years from here.

00:24:54.025 --> 00:24:56.186
It leads directly
to the other side

00:24:56.261 --> 00:24:57.489
of the expanse.

00:24:57.562 --> 00:25:00.053
We've been using it for years.

00:25:00.131 --> 00:25:01.996
That would get us
out of the Void

00:25:02.067 --> 00:25:04.331
and cut two years
off our journey home.

00:25:04.402 --> 00:25:05.767
Well, thank you again.

00:25:05.837 --> 00:25:07.202
I'm curious, Mr. Emck.

00:25:07.272 --> 00:25:08.864
What are you doing here...

00:25:08.940 --> 00:25:11.374
besides rescuing
starships in distress?

00:25:11.443 --> 00:25:14.879
Ah. I'm on a...
transport mission.

00:25:14.946 --> 00:25:16.208
My sensors tell me

00:25:16.281 --> 00:25:19.341
that one of the creatures
is still aboard your ship.

00:25:19.417 --> 00:25:21.146
It was injured
during the attack.

00:25:21.219 --> 00:25:22.584
Our Doctor's treating it.

00:25:22.654 --> 00:25:23.586
Why?

00:25:23.655 --> 00:25:24.917
Enough questions.

00:25:24.990 --> 00:25:28.016
Give me the creature
and I'll take you to the vortex.

00:25:28.093 --> 00:25:29.822
Well, my apologies, Mr. Emck,

00:25:29.895 --> 00:25:32.455
but I'd like to know
what's going on here.

00:25:32.531 --> 00:25:34.522
Are you at war
with these beings?

00:25:34.599 --> 00:25:36.430
None of your concern.

00:25:36.501 --> 00:25:38.696
Your vessel seems to be leaking

00:25:38.770 --> 00:25:41.136
large amounts
of theta radiation.

00:25:41.206 --> 00:25:44.869
What kind of transport mission
are you on exactly?

00:25:44.943 --> 00:25:48.037
My ship will depart
in two hours.

00:25:48.113 --> 00:25:50.547
Cooperate or stay behind.

00:25:50.615 --> 00:25:55.814
I won't be coming to your rescue
when the creatures return.

00:25:55.887 --> 00:25:58.378
I'm finished here.

00:26:06.298 --> 00:26:10.029
I think it's time we heard
the other side of the story.

00:26:14.406 --> 00:26:15.498
Watch your step.

00:26:15.574 --> 00:26:17.542
I've had to lower the lights.

00:26:17.609 --> 00:26:20.339
My patient is extremely
photosensitive.

00:26:20.412 --> 00:26:22.710
That could explain
why they dampened our power.

00:26:22.781 --> 00:26:23.748
My feelings exactly.

00:26:23.815 --> 00:26:24.907
From what I can tell,

00:26:25.050 --> 00:26:27.018
this life-form may be
indigenous to the Void.

00:26:27.085 --> 00:26:28.211
His physiology

00:26:28.286 --> 00:26:30.345
has evolved to survive
in complete darkness.

00:26:30.422 --> 00:26:31.753
His condition?

00:26:31.823 --> 00:26:32.915
Minor injuries...

00:26:32.991 --> 00:26:34.856
phaser wounds
to the chest and neck.

00:26:34.926 --> 00:26:37.087
But that's the least
of his problems.

00:26:37.162 --> 00:26:39.357
He's dying, Captain.

00:26:39.431 --> 00:26:43.299
Every organ is degrading
at the cellular level.

00:26:43.368 --> 00:26:45.632
Theta radiation poisoning.

00:26:45.704 --> 00:26:47.331
The final stages.

00:26:47.405 --> 00:26:50.465
My guess is he's been exposed
to it over a long period.

00:26:50.542 --> 00:26:51.873
There's nothing I can do.

00:26:51.943 --> 00:26:54.343
I'd like a word with him.

00:26:57.382 --> 00:27:00.647
I'm Kathryn Janeway,
Captain of this vessel.

00:27:00.719 --> 00:27:03.153
You are allies with the Malon.

00:27:03.221 --> 00:27:04.313
No.

00:27:04.389 --> 00:27:06.220
We're simply trying
to cross this region.

00:27:06.291 --> 00:27:08.759
We never met the Malon
before today.

00:27:08.827 --> 00:27:10.795
They will want me.

00:27:10.862 --> 00:27:13.160
Well, I have no intention
of giving you to them.

00:27:13.231 --> 00:27:14.493
You're not a captive here.

00:27:16.067 --> 00:27:16.999
Doctor.

00:27:17.068 --> 00:27:19.662
Are you at war with the Malon?

00:27:19.738 --> 00:27:21.603
Their ships are poison.

00:27:21.673 --> 00:27:22.731
The theta radiation.

00:27:22.807 --> 00:27:23.831
They're killing us.

00:27:23.908 --> 00:27:25.637
Why?
What do they want from you?

00:27:25.710 --> 00:27:27.871
Nothing.

00:27:27.946 --> 00:27:31.507
This will help
alleviate the pain.

00:27:31.583 --> 00:27:33.517
I don't understand.

00:27:33.585 --> 00:27:35.246
We were ignorant.

00:27:35.320 --> 00:27:36.878
We attacked you.

00:27:36.955 --> 00:27:38.047
Forgive us.

00:27:38.123 --> 00:27:39.852
Of course, but I
need to understand.

00:27:39.924 --> 00:27:41.915
You say the Malon are
killing your people,

00:27:42.027 --> 00:27:43.324
but there must be a reason.

00:27:43.395 --> 00:27:45.920
They're poisoning our space.

00:27:46.031 --> 00:27:47.692
We don't know why.

00:27:50.535 --> 00:27:51.866
He's in respiratory distress.

00:27:51.936 --> 00:27:53.699
We need to get him
back to his people.

00:27:53.772 --> 00:27:55.296
They might know
how to treat him.

00:27:55.373 --> 00:27:57.841
I will show you how.

00:27:57.909 --> 00:27:58.841
I need a workstation.

00:27:58.910 --> 00:28:00.070
Route it to the helm.

00:28:00.145 --> 00:28:03.637
If you enter the coordinates,
my pilot will set a course.

00:28:03.715 --> 00:28:05.546
I am grateful.

00:28:05.617 --> 00:28:07.175
Take the Bridge.

00:28:07.252 --> 00:28:08.719
I'll stay here.

00:28:08.787 --> 00:28:11.415
We still don't have a defense
against their dampening field.

00:28:11.489 --> 00:28:12.979
If they decide
to attack again...

00:28:13.058 --> 00:28:14.457
I'm confident they won't.

00:28:14.526 --> 00:28:16.858
Finally something
to put in my logbook.

00:28:19.397 --> 00:28:20.694
Tuvok.

00:28:28.173 --> 00:28:29.800
I need your advice.

00:28:29.874 --> 00:28:31.842
A first.

00:28:31.910 --> 00:28:35.505
Look, I realize
we're not exactly best friends.

00:28:35.580 --> 00:28:38.242
From day one, we've kept
each other at arm's length,

00:28:38.316 --> 00:28:40.876
but I've always respected
your judgment,

00:28:40.952 --> 00:28:43.079
and right now, I could use
a little Vulcan clarity.

00:28:43.154 --> 00:28:45.122
Proceed.

00:28:45.190 --> 00:28:46.623
It's the Captain.

00:28:46.691 --> 00:28:49.421
As you may have noticed, she's
isolated herself from the crew.

00:28:49.494 --> 00:28:50.722
She believes that she made

00:28:50.795 --> 00:28:52.524
an error in judgment
four years ago...

00:28:52.597 --> 00:28:54.690
that she's responsible
for stranding Voyager

00:28:54.766 --> 00:28:55.858
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:28:55.934 --> 00:28:57.094
She told you?

00:28:57.168 --> 00:28:58.499
No.

00:28:58.570 --> 00:29:02.233
I've been observing her behavior
for the past four years.

00:29:02.307 --> 00:29:04.775
Guilt has been
her constant companion.

00:29:04.843 --> 00:29:06.572
You've known her
longer than anyone.

00:29:06.644 --> 00:29:08.271
Have you ever
seen her like this?

00:29:08.346 --> 00:29:09.472
Only once.

00:29:09.547 --> 00:29:11.606
It was during her first year

00:29:11.683 --> 00:29:14.311
as a Commander
on the USS Billings.

00:29:14.385 --> 00:29:17.218
She sent an away team
to survey a volcanic moon.

00:29:17.288 --> 00:29:19.984
Their shuttle was damaged
by a magma eruption

00:29:20.058 --> 00:29:22.822
and three crew members
were severely injured.

00:29:22.894 --> 00:29:25.419
The next day, she returned
to the moon, alone,

00:29:25.497 --> 00:29:26.828
to complete the survey.

00:29:26.898 --> 00:29:28.456
She wanted the crew to know

00:29:28.533 --> 00:29:31.001
that their suffering
had not been in vain.

00:29:31.069 --> 00:29:32.593
She could have been killed.

00:29:32.670 --> 00:29:34.399
Seeking redemption.

00:29:34.472 --> 00:29:35.996
Precisely.

00:29:36.074 --> 00:29:39.510
Captain Janeway's methods
are unorthodox.

00:29:39.577 --> 00:29:41.511
It is her strength as a leader,

00:29:41.579 --> 00:29:45.015
but, unfortunately, it is also
her greatest weakness.

00:29:45.083 --> 00:29:47.142
Stubborn as a Klingon.

00:29:47.218 --> 00:29:48.845
To put it mildly.

00:29:48.920 --> 00:29:51.912
If she tries something
like that again,

00:29:52.056 --> 00:29:53.523
I want to be ready

00:29:53.591 --> 00:29:55.889
and I'm going
to need your support.

00:30:00.165 --> 00:30:02.531
We're at the coordinates.

00:30:02.600 --> 00:30:04.033
All stop.
Shields up.

00:30:04.102 --> 00:30:05.034
Tuvok.

00:30:05.103 --> 00:30:07.094
Nothing on sensors.

00:30:07.172 --> 00:30:08.639
Bridge to Captain.

00:30:08.706 --> 00:30:10.139
We've arrived.

00:30:10.208 --> 00:30:11.470
Stand by.

00:30:11.543 --> 00:30:15.536
They're here, but I must
tell them you are a friend.

00:30:15.613 --> 00:30:17.740
Your communications system?

00:30:25.190 --> 00:30:26.680
I'm picking up photonic surges.

00:30:26.758 --> 00:30:27.850
They're all around us.

00:30:31.930 --> 00:30:34.228
Captain, we've got company...
eight ships.

00:30:34.299 --> 00:30:35.766
12 more approaching.

00:30:35.834 --> 00:30:37.768
Let's run a full bio-scan.

00:30:37.836 --> 00:30:39.167
We have lived here

00:30:39.237 --> 00:30:42.570
for millions of years
undisturbed,

00:30:42.640 --> 00:30:44.540
until the Malon came.

00:30:44.609 --> 00:30:47.976
Captain, every one of them
appears to be suffering

00:30:48.079 --> 00:30:49.979
from theta radiation exposure.

00:30:50.114 --> 00:30:52.344
We tell them
they are killing us.

00:30:52.417 --> 00:30:54.681
They won't listen.

00:30:54.752 --> 00:30:56.982
We try to stop them.

00:30:57.088 --> 00:30:58.715
They're too strong.

00:30:58.790 --> 00:31:00.883
What about the vortex,
can you close it?

00:31:00.959 --> 00:31:01.891
Keep them out?

00:31:01.960 --> 00:31:04.793
We don't know how.

00:31:06.431 --> 00:31:08.865
Your ship is powerful.

00:31:08.933 --> 00:31:11.527
Your people resourceful.

00:31:11.603 --> 00:31:12.934
We need your help.

00:31:13.037 --> 00:31:14.436
Bridge to Captain.

00:31:14.505 --> 00:31:16.530
They're locking onto the alien
in Sick Bay.

00:31:16.608 --> 00:31:17.700
Lower the shields.

00:31:17.775 --> 00:31:20.073
Will you help us?!

00:31:34.259 --> 00:31:35.954
Poison.

00:31:36.027 --> 00:31:37.722
The vessel is ejecting
massive quantities

00:31:37.795 --> 00:31:38.887
of contaminated antimatter.

00:31:38.963 --> 00:31:40.726
Their cargo holds
are loaded with it...

00:31:40.798 --> 00:31:42.493
over 90 million isotons.

00:31:42.567 --> 00:31:44.364
Hail them.

00:31:44.435 --> 00:31:45.459
Captain.

00:31:45.536 --> 00:31:47.800
You've decided to join us.

00:31:47.872 --> 00:31:48.804
Send the creature to...

00:31:48.873 --> 00:31:49.897
That won't be possible.

00:31:49.974 --> 00:31:51.566
We've returned him
to his people.

00:31:51.643 --> 00:31:53.975
You wanted the life-form
because you were afraid

00:31:54.112 --> 00:31:56.979
we'd uncover your...
transport mission.

00:31:57.115 --> 00:31:58.980
I said this was
none of your concern.

00:31:59.083 --> 00:32:00.550
Well, it is now.

00:32:00.618 --> 00:32:02.745
You're using their space
as a dumping ground

00:32:02.820 --> 00:32:05.584
for your antimatter waste.
Why?

00:32:05.657 --> 00:32:09.923
My civilization produces
over six billion isotons

00:32:09.994 --> 00:32:12.656
of industrial byproduct
every day.

00:32:12.730 --> 00:32:15.927
This region is
a perfect disposal site.

00:32:16.000 --> 00:32:18.230
How convenient... for you.

00:32:18.303 --> 00:32:20.533
A spatial vortex
to the middle of nowhere,

00:32:20.605 --> 00:32:22.436
far away from your own system.

00:32:22.507 --> 00:32:24.771
Out of sight, out of mind.

00:32:24.842 --> 00:32:26.707
The problem is,
somebody lives here.

00:32:26.778 --> 00:32:27.904
One species.

00:32:27.979 --> 00:32:29.207
One's enough.

00:32:29.280 --> 00:32:31.271
We didn't come here
to debate the issue.

00:32:31.349 --> 00:32:34.250
We came here to offer
a peaceful solution.

00:32:34.319 --> 00:32:36.947
What kind of solution?

00:32:37.088 --> 00:32:39.215
My people use antimatter
as well,

00:32:39.290 --> 00:32:42.225
but we found ways
to purify the reactant

00:32:42.293 --> 00:32:44.158
so there's no toxic waste.

00:32:44.228 --> 00:32:45.957
We'll show you.

00:32:46.097 --> 00:32:48.588
Guide us through the vortex.

00:32:48.666 --> 00:32:49.963
We can meet with your scientists

00:32:50.034 --> 00:32:52.366
on the other side,
exchange information.

00:32:52.437 --> 00:32:54.428
Show me now.

00:32:57.041 --> 00:32:58.633
Stand by for transport.

00:33:00.378 --> 00:33:02.505
Commander, take our
guest to Engineering

00:33:02.580 --> 00:33:04.172
and give him a demonstration.

00:33:04.248 --> 00:33:06.273
Let's turn our sensors
on that vortex.

00:33:06.351 --> 00:33:08.285
I want to know exactly
how it works...

00:33:08.353 --> 00:33:11.288
just in case diplomacy fails.

00:33:11.356 --> 00:33:13.654
Do you intend to destroy it?

00:33:16.861 --> 00:33:19.261
The residual antimatter's
then processed

00:33:19.330 --> 00:33:20.592
in a transkinetic chamber

00:33:20.665 --> 00:33:22.929
where it's broken down
on a subatomic level.

00:33:23.034 --> 00:33:25.400
What about the theta radiation?

00:33:25.470 --> 00:33:29.531
Oh, it's absorbed by a series
of radiometric converters.

00:33:29.607 --> 00:33:31.234
We recycle the energy...

00:33:31.309 --> 00:33:33.300
use it to power everything

00:33:33.378 --> 00:33:35.608
from life support
to replicators.

00:33:35.680 --> 00:33:38.945
We don't have this kind
of conversion technology.

00:33:39.050 --> 00:33:40.278
Our scans of your freighter

00:33:40.351 --> 00:33:41.943
show that you have
plasma manifolds.

00:33:42.053 --> 00:33:43.816
The engineering
principles are the same.

00:33:43.888 --> 00:33:45.947
We're not saying this
won't take some effort.

00:33:46.057 --> 00:33:48.423
You're looking at several
months of retrofitting,

00:33:48.493 --> 00:33:50.222
depending on the size
of your fleet.

00:33:50.294 --> 00:33:51.556
All the schematics are here

00:33:51.629 --> 00:33:53.529
and we'd be willing
to work with you...

00:33:53.598 --> 00:33:54.656
get you started.

00:33:54.732 --> 00:33:56.962
We can even provide you
with some converters.

00:33:59.003 --> 00:34:00.732
Ingenious design.

00:34:00.805 --> 00:34:03.968
Our engineers would be pleased.

00:34:05.343 --> 00:34:09.507
This would solve a lot
of problems on my world.

00:34:09.580 --> 00:34:14.916
Unfortunately, it would also
put me out of business.

00:34:15.019 --> 00:34:16.281
Sorry?

00:34:16.354 --> 00:34:19.755
Your technology would throw
the waste-export industry

00:34:19.824 --> 00:34:20.916
into chaos.

00:34:21.025 --> 00:34:22.993
Before long, I'd be obsolete.

00:34:25.696 --> 00:34:30.599
Oh, I came here hoping
your claims were exaggerated,

00:34:30.668 --> 00:34:33.136
but I can see they're not.

00:34:35.373 --> 00:34:38.399
You can keep your solution.

00:34:38.476 --> 00:34:39.443
You lying...

00:34:39.510 --> 00:34:40.499
B'Elanna.

00:34:40.578 --> 00:34:41.943
We went through
this whole song and dance,

00:34:42.046 --> 00:34:43.775
and he never had any intention
of working with us.

00:34:43.848 --> 00:34:44.940
That's not important.

00:34:45.049 --> 00:34:47.313
What matters is
that we're talking now.

00:34:47.385 --> 00:34:50.821
We're proposing changes,
some of them difficult,

00:34:50.888 --> 00:34:54.255
but progress can also bring
new opportunities.

00:34:54.325 --> 00:34:56.987
Given time, this could turn
to your advantage.

00:34:58.329 --> 00:35:00.456
I already have the advantage...

00:35:00.531 --> 00:35:01.657
the vortex.

00:35:01.732 --> 00:35:04.667
No one knows about it
except me and my crew.

00:35:04.735 --> 00:35:10.037
By ejecting my cargo here,
I cut expenses in half.

00:35:10.108 --> 00:35:12.599
I won't sacrifice that.

00:35:12.677 --> 00:35:13.609
I guess mass murder

00:35:13.678 --> 00:35:15.612
doesn't factor
into your profit margin.

00:35:15.680 --> 00:35:18.877
You care so much
about these creatures, stay.

00:35:21.018 --> 00:35:23.043
I'm sorry you won't
listen to reason,

00:35:23.121 --> 00:35:25.612
but don't expect us
to walk away from this.

00:35:25.690 --> 00:35:27.817
You've scanned my vessel.

00:35:27.892 --> 00:35:30.019
You've seen my firepower.

00:35:30.094 --> 00:35:34.827
You wouldn't survive ten seconds
in a conflict with me.

00:35:34.899 --> 00:35:36.992
Get him out of here.

00:35:40.705 --> 00:35:41.672
Ah!

00:35:46.777 --> 00:35:47.744
Options?

00:35:47.812 --> 00:35:49.473
We fight our way past them...

00:35:49.547 --> 00:35:51.208
navigate the vortex on our own.

00:35:51.282 --> 00:35:52.476
Once we're on the other side,

00:35:52.550 --> 00:35:55.280
we contact the Malon authorities
and blow the whistle on Emck.

00:35:55.353 --> 00:35:57.184
We give them
the reclamation technology

00:35:57.255 --> 00:35:58.688
and continue on our way home.

00:35:58.756 --> 00:35:59.723
Exactly.

00:35:59.790 --> 00:36:01.849
Even if we did
get through the vortex,

00:36:01.926 --> 00:36:02.858
there's no guarantee

00:36:02.927 --> 00:36:04.451
the Malon will
do the right thing...

00:36:04.529 --> 00:36:06.463
if Mr. Emck is any indication.

00:36:06.531 --> 00:36:08.897
As long as this vortex exists,

00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:11.764
the inhabitants
of this region are at risk.

00:36:13.571 --> 00:36:15.232
Any chance we could destroy it?

00:36:15.306 --> 00:36:16.330
I believe so,

00:36:16.407 --> 00:36:17.567
but there's a catch.

00:36:17.642 --> 00:36:19.906
We'll have to collapse it
from this end

00:36:20.044 --> 00:36:22.911
where it's dimensional
radius is weakest.

00:36:22.980 --> 00:36:25.949
We'd be closing
our shortcut out of here.

00:36:27.518 --> 00:36:28.917
Two more years in the Void.

00:36:29.020 --> 00:36:30.112
I can live with that.

00:36:30.188 --> 00:36:32.816
But I'm not sure I can.

00:36:32.890 --> 00:36:34.824
Four years ago,

00:36:34.892 --> 00:36:38.453
I destroyed the Caretaker's
Array to protect the Ocampa.

00:36:38.529 --> 00:36:39.928
That "act of compassion"

00:36:40.031 --> 00:36:42.522
stranded this crew
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:36:42.600 --> 00:36:44.329
I'm not about
to give that order again.

00:36:44.402 --> 00:36:45.767
This situation is
a little different.

00:36:45.836 --> 00:36:47.394
Oh, it's close enough.

00:36:47.471 --> 00:36:50.463
I'm asking this crew
to make too big a sacrifice.

00:36:50.541 --> 00:36:52.941
I won't make that same mistake.

00:36:53.077 --> 00:36:55.875
If you have another option,
I'm listening.

00:36:57.982 --> 00:36:59.916
Chakotay,

00:36:59.984 --> 00:37:02.578
there's no one I trust
more than you.

00:37:02.653 --> 00:37:04.621
You're a fine First Officer.

00:37:07.325 --> 00:37:09.793
Are you ready
to Captain this ship?

00:37:11.662 --> 00:37:12.686
Yes.

00:37:12.763 --> 00:37:14.025
Assemble the crew.

00:37:28.212 --> 00:37:30.646
Captain on the Bridge.

00:37:30.715 --> 00:37:32.683
At ease.

00:37:43.361 --> 00:37:44.760
Harry, how have you been?

00:37:44.829 --> 00:37:45.921
Just fine, ma'am.

00:37:46.030 --> 00:37:47.190
Good.

00:37:50.034 --> 00:37:51.365
We've missed you, Captain.

00:37:51.435 --> 00:37:52.561
Likewise.

00:37:52.637 --> 00:37:54.127
I'll make this brief.

00:37:54.205 --> 00:37:57.106
Your orders are to proceed
to the vortex.

00:37:57.174 --> 00:37:59.199
Use whatever means necessary

00:37:59.277 --> 00:38:02.337
to fight your way
past the Malon freighter.

00:38:02.413 --> 00:38:04.813
I'll stay behind
in a shuttlecraft

00:38:04.882 --> 00:38:06.509
and destroy the vortex.

00:38:06.584 --> 00:38:09.144
Tuvok, I'll need
a class-2 shuttle

00:38:09.220 --> 00:38:11.245
armed with photon torpedoes.

00:38:11.322 --> 00:38:13.256
Tom, set a course for...

00:38:13.324 --> 00:38:14.450
Forget it.

00:38:14.525 --> 00:38:16.425
We're not going to let you
die out here.

00:38:16.494 --> 00:38:18.086
Have a little faith, B'Elanna.

00:38:18.162 --> 00:38:21.029
I'll have a shuttle, plenty
of rations. I'll survive.

00:38:21.098 --> 00:38:23.157
Alone in the Delta Quadrant?

00:38:23.234 --> 00:38:24.565
No offense, but...

00:38:24.635 --> 00:38:25.795
I've made my decision.

00:38:25.870 --> 00:38:26.894
What about us?

00:38:27.004 --> 00:38:28.164
Don't we have a say?

00:38:28.239 --> 00:38:29.399
He's right, Captain.

00:38:29.473 --> 00:38:30.906
I'd be willing
to brave this Void

00:38:31.008 --> 00:38:32.532
if it meant keeping you with us.

00:38:37.014 --> 00:38:39.539
Tom... set a course.

00:38:41.986 --> 00:38:43.749
Lieutenant, I gave you an order.

00:38:48.693 --> 00:38:51.890
I can't follow that order,
ma'am.

00:38:51.962 --> 00:38:53.486
Harry, take the helm.

00:38:56.967 --> 00:38:58.832
I'm sorry, Captain.

00:39:11.315 --> 00:39:13.283
I will not comply.

00:39:18.356 --> 00:39:20.085
What's a hologram to do?

00:39:20.157 --> 00:39:22.990
As you can see, you're
not the only one

00:39:23.060 --> 00:39:25.688
who's had time
to evaluate the past.

00:39:25.763 --> 00:39:27.492
Yes, I can see that.

00:39:31.001 --> 00:39:35.802
You realize you could all
be hanged for mutiny.

00:39:35.873 --> 00:39:38.171
Looks like we need
another option.

00:39:38.242 --> 00:39:41.871
We fire torpedoes the instant
we cross the threshold.

00:39:41.946 --> 00:39:43.311
As the vortex
begins to collapse,

00:39:43.381 --> 00:39:44.370
we jump into high warp.

00:39:44.448 --> 00:39:46.439
There'll be a massive
shock wave on our tail.

00:39:46.517 --> 00:39:48.144
I'll reinforce
the aft shielding.

00:39:48.219 --> 00:39:50.278
There's still one obstacle...
the Malon.

00:39:50.354 --> 00:39:52.345
Antimatter waste has
weakened the bulkhead

00:39:52.423 --> 00:39:53.788
surrounding their cargo hold.

00:39:53.858 --> 00:39:55.917
A direct phaser strike
should disable them.

00:39:56.060 --> 00:39:56.924
Poetic justice.

00:39:57.061 --> 00:39:57.925
Indeed.

00:39:58.062 --> 00:39:59.427
You realize it will reduce

00:39:59.497 --> 00:40:01.055
our chance of getting through.

00:40:01.132 --> 00:40:03.123
Chance is irrelevant.
We will succeed.

00:40:03.200 --> 00:40:04.929
A vote of Borg confidence.

00:40:05.035 --> 00:40:06.832
Who could argue with that?

00:40:06.904 --> 00:40:07.928
All right.

00:40:08.038 --> 00:40:09.300
Back to your stations.

00:40:09.373 --> 00:40:10.431
Let's do it.

00:40:10.508 --> 00:40:12.942
Red Alert.
Set a course for the vortex.

00:40:13.043 --> 00:40:14.943
All hands to battle stations.

00:40:15.045 --> 00:40:16.307
You told them.

00:40:16.380 --> 00:40:17.642
They knew coming in.

00:40:17.715 --> 00:40:19.546
Let's just say I wouldn't be

00:40:19.617 --> 00:40:21.847
a fine First Officer
if I hadn't.

00:40:39.336 --> 00:40:40.598
Return fire.

00:40:40.671 --> 00:40:42.605
Hit them
with everything we've got.

00:40:48.679 --> 00:40:50.306
Their shields are holding.

00:40:50.381 --> 00:40:51.370
Open a channel.

00:40:51.449 --> 00:40:52.473
This is Voyager.

00:40:52.550 --> 00:40:55.018
Stand down your weapons
and fall back.

00:40:57.755 --> 00:40:59.416
I'll take that as a "no."

00:40:59.490 --> 00:41:01.117
The vortex?

00:41:01.192 --> 00:41:02.921
Two million kilometers
dead ahead.

00:41:03.027 --> 00:41:04.187
Bridge to Engineering.

00:41:04.261 --> 00:41:05.751
We're approaching the vortex.

00:41:05.830 --> 00:41:07.695
Bring the aft shielding
on line.

00:41:07.765 --> 00:41:08.732
Acknowledged.

00:41:08.799 --> 00:41:10.460
See you on the other side.

00:41:13.170 --> 00:41:14.159
Status?

00:41:14.238 --> 00:41:16.172
The port nacelle's
been ruptured.

00:41:16.240 --> 00:41:17.434
We're venting plasma.

00:41:17.508 --> 00:41:19.738
Can you get us out of here
on one engine, Tom?

00:41:19.810 --> 00:41:21.141
I think so.

00:41:21.212 --> 00:41:22.679
Torpedoes armed and ready.

00:41:22.746 --> 00:41:23.838
On my order, Tuvok.

00:41:23.914 --> 00:41:25.779
We'll only get one shot at this.

00:41:25.850 --> 00:41:27.647
They're firing spatial charges.

00:41:27.718 --> 00:41:28.776
Evade them.

00:41:38.696 --> 00:41:40.823
Captain Proton to the rescue.

00:41:43.100 --> 00:41:44.431
I'll explain later.

00:41:44.502 --> 00:41:46.663
The vortex is in visual range.

00:41:46.737 --> 00:41:47.965
Time to intercept?

00:41:48.072 --> 00:41:48.970
47 seconds.

00:41:49.073 --> 00:41:50.472
Steady as she goes.

00:41:50.541 --> 00:41:52.338
Keep laying down fire.

00:41:53.644 --> 00:41:55.475
Direct hit! Starboard nacelle!

00:41:55.546 --> 00:41:56.843
Both engines are off-line!

00:41:56.914 --> 00:41:58.142
We're riding on inertia.

00:41:58.215 --> 00:42:00.308
One more hit
and we're dead in the water.

00:42:00.384 --> 00:42:02.545
Without warp drive, we'll never
outrun the shock wave.

00:42:02.620 --> 00:42:04.212
Tuvok, can you reinforce
the aft shields

00:42:04.288 --> 00:42:05.255
with our main deflector?

00:42:05.322 --> 00:42:06.254
I believe so.

00:42:06.323 --> 00:42:07.517
Do it.

00:42:07.591 --> 00:42:10.185
We're going to ride
that shock wave out of here...

00:42:10.261 --> 00:42:12.024
let it push us
to the other side.

00:42:12.096 --> 00:42:13.222
Adjusting shield harmonics.

00:42:14.298 --> 00:42:15.925
Captain.

00:42:18.502 --> 00:42:20.766
They intend to block our path.

00:42:20.838 --> 00:42:22.237
20 seconds.

00:42:22.306 --> 00:42:23.432
Prepare to fire.

00:42:23.507 --> 00:42:24.769
That may not be necessary.

00:42:32.816 --> 00:42:34.943
The freighter is moving
to combat the aliens.

00:42:35.085 --> 00:42:36.950
They're trying to distract
the Malon...

00:42:37.087 --> 00:42:38.213
give us the upper hand.

00:42:38.289 --> 00:42:40.086
Ten seconds.

00:42:40.157 --> 00:42:41.454
The freighter's shields
are weakening.

00:42:41.525 --> 00:42:43.550
Target their cargo hold.

00:42:43.627 --> 00:42:46.255
Time to take out the garbage.

00:42:54.338 --> 00:42:55.703
We're crossing the threshold.

00:42:55.773 --> 00:42:57.240
Torpedoes.

00:43:03.314 --> 00:43:05.305
Shock wave approaching.
600 meters.

00:43:05.382 --> 00:43:06.314
500...

00:43:06.383 --> 00:43:07.315
400...

00:43:07.384 --> 00:43:08.851
Aft shields at maximum.

00:43:08.919 --> 00:43:10.546
All hands brace for impact.

00:43:17.962 --> 00:43:20.260
Pressure is building
on the outer hull.

00:43:20.331 --> 00:43:21.923
Shields weakening.

00:43:25.936 --> 00:43:27.130
We're clear.

00:43:27.204 --> 00:43:28.933
The vortex has been destroyed.

00:43:29.006 --> 00:43:30.303
Are we out of the Void?

00:43:30.374 --> 00:43:31.534
Not yet.

00:43:31.609 --> 00:43:34.237
That little maneuver
brought us up a bit short.

00:43:34.311 --> 00:43:37.280
We're still 200,000 kilometers
from the boundary.

00:43:37.348 --> 00:43:38.610
On screen.

00:43:43.921 --> 00:43:45.548
Maintain course.

00:44:02.072 --> 00:44:03.835
There.

00:44:03.907 --> 00:44:05.033
What?

00:44:05.109 --> 00:44:07.373
I saw something.

00:44:07.444 --> 00:44:09.241
A star.

00:44:09.313 --> 00:44:11.406
Remind me to check
your eyesight.

00:44:44.682 --> 00:44:48.243
Harry,
what do you see out there?

00:44:48.318 --> 00:44:54.257
I see a densely-packed region
with thousands of star systems.

00:44:55.693 --> 00:44:57.718
Looks pretty lively.

00:45:01.865 --> 00:45:04.265
Full speed ahead.
